# Text files are stored and checked out as LF on every OS.
#
# This machine's git has core.autocrlf=true, which would hand a fresh clone
# CRLF working copies while this tree is LF. The checks in tests/ read files
# line by line (PublishCheck's allowlist and secret scan, DocsCheck's claim
# extraction), so a silent CRLF checkout would change what they see. Pinning
# LF here makes every clone byte-identical to the tree these were written
# against. MSVC handles LF throughout, so nothing is lost on Windows.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never normalised, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
